206 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 138 0 R
/T (Agriculture is increasingly supported by digital technologies, yet farmers may find it difficult to interpret crop symptoms, weather conditions, soil information, and market signals in one place. Annadatha AI is proposed as an AI-powered smart agriculture web application that brings crop- image analysis and farm-context information into a single interface. The project is designed to accept crop photographs and structured details such as crop type, growth stage, cultivated area, planting date, soil characteristics, fertilizer and irrigation practices, and available weather information. An AI analysis service is intended to return a structured assessment covering crop identification, visible disease indications, estimated severity, possible yield outlook, risk factors, and practical recommendations. )
/E (Agriculture is increasingly supported by digital technologies, yet farmers may find it difficult to interpret crop symptoms, weather conditions, soil information, and market signals in one place. Annadatha AI is proposed as an AI-powered smart agriculture web application that brings crop- image analysis and farm-context information into a single interface. The project is designed to accept crop photographs and structured details such as crop type, growth stage, cultivated area, planting date, soil characteristics, fertilizer and irrigation practices, and available weather information. An AI analysis service is intended to return a structured assessment covering crop identification, visible disease indications, estimated severity, possible yield outlook, risk factors, and practical recommendations. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 138 0 R
/T (The application is developed using a modern web stack based on React, TypeScript, and TanStack Start. Server-side functions are used to validate requests and keep provider credentials out of browser code. The AI integration is designed to try Google Gemini first and use OpenRouter as a fallback when the primary provider is unavailable. Responses must be validated before being shown to users, and failures should produce a friendly message rather than raw provider errors. Additional planned or integrated areas include multilingual UI, location-aware weather, crop and analysis history, market information, and learning-oriented AR/MR experiences. )
/E (The application is developed using a modern web stack based on React, TypeScript, and TanStack Start. Server-side functions are used to validate requests and keep provider credentials out of browser code. The AI integration is designed to try Google Gemini first and use OpenRouter as a fallback when the primary provider is unavailable. Responses must be validated before being shown to users, and failures should produce a friendly message rather than raw provider errors. Additional planned or integrated areas include multilingual UI, location-aware weather, crop and analysis history, market information, and learning-oriented AR/MR experiences. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 138 0 R
/T (This Phase I report describes the problem, objectives, related concepts, architecture, requirements, proposed modules, testing approach, risks, and future work. Since external AI models and live data providers can change availability, the report distinguishes intended functionality from results that require confirmation through actual deployment and testing. AI- generated crop advice is decision support only and should not replace local agricultural experts, laboratory soil tests, or verified product-label guidance. )
/E (This Phase I report describes the problem, objectives, related concepts, architecture, requirements, proposed modules, testing approach, risks, and future work. Since external AI models and live data providers can change availability, the report distinguishes intended functionality from results that require confirmation through actual deployment and testing. AI- generated crop advice is decision support only and should not replace local agricultural experts, laboratory soil tests, or verified product-label guidance. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
