/T (Computervisioncan identifyvisual patterns in leaf and crop images, including spots, discoloration, lesions, and deformation. Image classification assigns an image to a category, while object detection or segmentation can localize affected regions. Performance depends on image quality, training data, crop variety, lighting, background, and whether the image shows symptoms at a useful stage. A production-grade diagnosis system should be evaluated using labelled images captured under realistic field conditions. )
