1636 0 obj
<<
/Title (Agriculture is increasingly supported by digital technologies, yet farmers may find it difficult to interpret crop symptoms, weather conditions, soil information, and market signals in one place. Annadatha AI is proposed as an AI-powered smart agriculture web application that brings crop- image analysis and farm-context information into a single interface. The project is designed to accept crop photographs and structured details such as crop type, growth stage, cultivated area, planting date, soil characteristics, fertilizer and irrigation practices, and available weather information. An AI analysis service is intended to return a structured assessment covering crop identification, visible disease indications, estimated severity, possible yield outlook, risk factors, and practical recommendations.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1620 0 R
/Next 1661 0 R
>>
endobj
1637 0 obj
<<
/Title (This Phase I report describes the problem, objectives, related concepts, architecture, requirements, proposed modules, testing approach, risks, and future work. Since external AI models and live data providers can change availability, the report distinguishes intended functionality from results that require confirmation through actual deployment and testing. AI- generated crop advice is decision support only and should not replace local agricultural experts, laboratory soil tests, or verified product-label guidance.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1620 0 R
/Prev 1661 0 R
>>
endobj
